# The image's build context is an allowlist: what building and trying Tide reads, as a public
# clone has it. Everything else stays out: .git and its local configuration, the .beads ledger,
# agent and editor state, credentials such as .env files, and build outputs. Untracked files
# without a leading dot under the allowed directories do reach the builder, so build images to
# publish from a fresh clone.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!flake.nix
!flake.lock
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!README.md
!crates
!conformance
!examples
!benchmarks
!demo
!docs

# Local and ignored files inside the allowed directories (.gitignore's patterns, and dotfiles).
**/target
**/debug
**/result
**/result-*
**/*.rs.bk
**/*.pdb
**/mutants.out*
**/.*
